        <body>
            <div xml:id="d668">

                <pb facs="0706" n="588" xml:id="pg588"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">312.1722 Sandino/39</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morrow</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-06-28">June 28, 1929</date>.<lb/>[Received July
                        3.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1718</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that according
                    to a press statement, General Augusto Sandino, the Nicaraguan bandit, arrived in
                    Mexico day before yesterday, entering at Tapachula, Chiapas, from Guatemala, and
                    that he is said to be en route to Yucatan, where he will fix his residence.</p>
                <p>Mr. Sierra, of the Foreign Office, today renewed to a member of the Embassy the
                    previous assurance that Sandino would not be allowed to come to Mexico City and
                    stated that if through any circumstance he should come to the capital, no
                    demonstration of any kind in his behalf would be permitted.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dwight W. Morrow</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
